quests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"63ed505dd9571aa9ead3d965dc7407576efc09c28f27f40e5ea6b16443e35c9c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":47226,"output_tokens":1753,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"5759e95dbc549fb877852ec0ae6500a6c127924bbb54431eb216d002f3d84de4"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":111884,"output_tokens":3035,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Widen the terraform AC to enumerate removing the now-orphaned Lambda env vars (SEED_RATES, RATE_OVERRIDES, UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K, RATE_WINDOW_DAYS) and their backing variables/locals (bedrock_cap_seed_rates, bedrock_cap_unknown_rate_per_1k, bedrock_cap_rate_overrides), and reconcile the 'plan shows only threshold/warning changes' assertion with those removals.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["bedrock_spend_cap.tf:441 `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K = tostring(var.bedrock_cap_unknown_rate_per_1k)`","bedrock_spend_cap.tf:443-444 `RATE_OVERRIDES = jsonencode(local.bedrock_cap_rate_overrides)` / `SEED_RATES = jsonencode(local.bedrock_cap_seed_rates)`","bedrock_spend_cap.tf:436 `RATE_WINDOW_DAYS = \"60\"` — dead once _refresh_rates is deleted","handler AC removes SEED_RATES, RATE_OVERRIDES, UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K from the module","variables bedrock_cap_seed_rates (54), bedrock_cap_unknown_rate_per_1k (70), local bedrock_cap_rate_overrides (129) become unused"],"finding":"The terraform edit is under-scoped: the handler AC removes env-sourced names (SEED_RATES, RATE_OVERRIDES, UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K) and RATE_WINDOW_DAYS becomes dead once rate-derivation is deleted, but these are all wired in bedrock_spend_cap.tf as Lambda environment{} vars fed by variables bedrock_cap_seed_rates / bedrock_cap_unknown_rate_per_1k and local bedrock_cap_rate_overrides. The plan's terraform AC restricts the change to threshold/warning values and asserts terraform plan shows ONLY those env changes, which contradicts removing the orphaned env/variables/locals.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f286c1966251ab0f7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'Threshold and warning values in infra/terraform/bedrock_spend_cap.tf match the design note. Checked: terraform plan shows only those env changes.'","norm_id":"nf5fbc08d63a50cb5","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["terraform plan after the code change proposes removing SEED_RATES/RATE_OVERRIDES/UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K/RATE_WINDOW_DAYS env entries, violating the 'only those env changes' assertion","orphaned variables/locals linger and trip lint or a future reviewer"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Restate the terraform AC as: add CEILING config + updated threshold/warning; delete the SEED_RATES/RATE_OVERRIDES/UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K/RATE_WINDOW_DAYS env entries and their unused variables/locals; terraform plan shows exactly that env delta and nothing else.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the README AC to also remove the now-obsolete 'prices derived from bills', seed-rate fallback order, and UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K sections, not just add the over-estimate/upper-bound prose.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["README.md:41 '**Prices are derived from this account's own bills**, not a hardcoded table.'","README.md:49-55 lists the seed-rate/`local.bedrock_cap_seed_rates`/`UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K` fallback order being deleted","plan README AC: 'The README states the accepted over-estimate, the effective-cap band qualitatively, and that the figure is an upper bound' — additive only"],"finding":"README.md is an in-repo consumer whose current 'How spend is measured' section documents the deleted pricing-derivation layer, the seed-rate fallback order (citing local.bedrock_cap_seed_rates), and UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K fail-closed behavior. The README AC only adds over-estimate/upper-bound prose and does not enumerate removing this now-false content.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5b30eee771fafce","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — README AC; infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md lines 41-59","norm_id":"nb6f5af9936c54d0a","priority":0.875,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After the change the README still describes cost/quantity rate derivation and seed fallbacks that no longer exist, contradicting the ceiling design"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the mechanism distinguishes a CloudWatch metrics-delivery gap (must NOT release the deny) from genuine zero Bedrock usage (must release, including the 00:00 UTC auto-release on this tick), so AC-5's empty-read guard does not deadlock the normal daily release.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC5: 'The cap does not release on a tick where every CloudWatch query returned no datapoints. Checked: a test asserting the deny stays attached on an empty read.'","tf: schedule 'Drives the Bedrock daily spend cap; also performs the 00:00 UTC release' — the release depends on a genuinely-empty CloudWatch read at day rollover","handler release condition: 'if any_attached and spend < THRESHOLD_USD and not signal_unavailable' — an all-empty undimensioned read yields total 0, not None, and signal_unavailable is false, so today it releases"],"finding":"AC-5 ('cap does not release on a tick where every CloudWatch query returned no datapoints') does not distinguish a metrics-delivery gap from genuine zero spend, which is the normal release condition — including the 00:00 UTC auto-release that runs on this same 5-minute tick. As worded, the mechanism would refuse to release the deny on an idle account or a fresh UTC day with no usage yet.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7fb9b9d600b48ded","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, bullet 5 ('The cap does not release on a tick where every CloudWatch query returned no datapoints'); interacts with handler.py release path (lines 718-730) and bedrock_spend_cap.tf:462 (tick 'also performs the 00:00 UTC release')","norm_id":"nc307436fe4ebc2b2","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["New UTC day: no Bedrock usage yet, all four undimensioned queries return no datapoints — the deny must release, but AC5 says keep it attached","Idle account with the cap tripped yesterday's spend now settled to 0 today — release must occur"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Gate the empty-read no-release on a corroborating signal rather than on datapoint count alone: e.g. treat an all-empty CloudWatch read as unavailable/hold ONLY when a query error or explicit outage is observed, or when CE for the day is nonzero/unavailable; when CE confirms 0 (or is available and 0) for the current day, permit release. State this discriminator in the Approach and reflect it in the AC-5 test (empty read + CE=0 -> release allowed; empty read + CE nonzero/unavailable -> deny stays).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State whether the now-unused SEED_RATES/RATE_OVERRIDES/UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K/RATE_WINDOW_DAYS Lambda env entries and their `variable`/`locals` declarations in bedrock_spend_cap.tf are removed, and reconcile that with AC-6's 'terraform plan shows only those env changes'.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC-1 lists SEED_RATES, RATE_OVERRIDES, UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K as names that must be 'gone from the module'","bedrock_spend_cap.tf declares `variable \"bedrock_cap_seed_rates\"`, `variable \"bedrock_cap_unknown_rate_per_1k\"`, and passes `UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K`, `RATE_OVERRIDES`, `SEED_RATES`, `RATE_WINDOW_DAYS` into the Lambda environment","AC-6 constrains the plan to 'only those env changes' (threshold/warning) — silent on removing the four now-dead env vars and their variable/locals blocks"],"finding":"The plan deletes the pricing layer's use of SEED_RATES, RATE_OVERRIDES, UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K and RATE_WINDOW_DAYS from handler.py, but the Terraform (bedrock_spend_cap.tf) still declares the variables bedrock_cap_seed_rates and bedrock_cap_unknown_rate_per_1k, the locals bedrock_cap_seed_rates/bedrock_cap_rate_overrides, and the environment entries UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K/RATE_OVERRIDES/SEED_RATES/RATE_WINDOW_DAYS. AC-6 only calls for threshold and warning env changes and asserts 'terraform plan shows only those env changes', so the plan does not account for removing these now-orphaned declarations — leaving dead IaC config that either contradicts that AC or persists unused variables.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fae9a157443dea966","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria bullet 6 ('Threshold and warning values ... terraform plan shows only those env changes'); infra/terraform/bedrock_spend_cap.tf lines 54-74, 119-132, 441-444","norm_id":"n31627cf73e7caab7","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer runs terraform plan expecting only THRESHOLD_USD/WARN_THRESHOLD_USD to change but sees no cleanup of orphaned env vars, or the dead variables/locals linger as drift"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend AC-6 to require removal of the orphaned env vars (UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K, RATE_OVERRIDES, SEED_RATES, RATE_WINDOW_DAYS) and the corresponding `variable`/`locals` blocks, and update the expected `terraform plan` diff to include those deletions alongside the threshold/warning changes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure disposition per enforcement arm when a CloudWatch GetMetricData or CE GetCostAndUsage call raises (not merely returns empty): whether the tick fails closed (deny stays attached) and which disposition wins when only one arm of max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend) is available.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract","T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC5 covers only 'a tick where every CloudWatch query returned no datapoints' — an empty result, not an API exception","'spend = max( ... CloudWatch Sum * CEILING, ce_spend )' composes two external-read arms with no stated disposition when either read raises","The plan removes the fail-closed fallback rate (UNKNOWN_RATE_PER_1K) and the ' (estimated)' path, so the prior fail-closed mechanism is gone and its replacement for the error (not empty) case is unstated"],"finding":"The plan states the disposition for an empty CloudWatch read (AC5: deny stays attached, fail-closed) but does not state the disposition when a CloudWatch GetMetricData or Cost Explorer GetCostAndUsage call itself raises an exception (throttle, timeout, 5xx). Since enforcement is max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend), if the CE arm errors the plan does not say whether enforcement proceeds on the ceiling estimate alone or fails closed, nor which disposition wins when one arm of the max() is unavailable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f43524a870593e912","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria (max(ceiling_estimate, ce_spend); AC5 empty-read)","norm_id":"n7fb20cb6857bba8a","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC and test: on any exception from the metered or CE read, the tick fails closed (deny remains attached, no release), mirroring the empty-read guarantee; document that a missing CE arm never lets the ceiling estimate alone release the cap.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the machine-local figures policy with the 'recorded real CE payloads committed to the repo' AC: state whether committed fixtures must be sanitized/synthesized (rates/spend redacted) or whether the repo is exempt from the public-mirror constraint.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["COH"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.198,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Figures: 'Machine-local policy bars spend totals, unit costs, budgets, cap thresholds and bill figures from the tracker, because the tickets branch auto-pushes to the public GitHub mirror.'","AC: 'Tests run off recorded real CE and list_metrics payloads committed to the repo, the CE one containing CamelCase, snake_case, _Global and a non-token usage type.'","A recorded CE payload inherently contains dollar spend amounts per service/usage type."],"finding":"The 'Figures' 